course: dictionary
lesson: 264
title: Amazement and surprise
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Amazement is the feeling you get when something is so wonderful, or so hard to believe, that you are very surprised. It is a strong word for surprise. You can feel a little surprised by a sock that turns up in the fridge, but amazement is much bigger than that.
explain: Look for the clues around the word. Writers often show amazement through what people do: «stared in amazement» means someone looked at something with wide eyes and did not move. «A look of amazement» shows the feeling on a face.
explain: The phrase «to his amazement» tells you what happened and how the character felt about it. Jake tells a teacher instead of fighting, and «to his amazement, it works». Jake did not expect it to work, so he was amazed. Ask yourself: what happened, and was it hard to believe?
fact: Amazement is a noun, a name for a feeling.
fact: Amazement means being very surprised because something is wonderful or hard to believe.
fact: Useful phrases include «in amazement», «to my amazement» and «a look of amazement».
fact: «To his amazement» means something surprising happened, and he did not expect it.
fact: Amazement is uncountable, so you say «with amazement», not «with an amazement».
exercise: In «to his amazement, it works», how does Jake feel? | Scared of the older boys | Bored and tired | Angry that the teacher was there | *Very surprised that it worked
exercise: Hannah «stared in amazement» at the sky. What does this phrase show? | She was hungry for lunch | *She was very surprised by something wonderful | She was falling asleep | She was cross with the weather
exercise: Which would most likely cause amazement? | *Watching a magician make a coin vanish | Waiting for the bus in the rain | Eating cereal for breakfast | Tidying your bedroom
test: Which word is closest in meaning to amazement? | *Surprise | Anger | Hunger | Sleepiness
test: Which sentence shows amazement? | He yawned and closed his book. | She put the kettle on for tea. | He wiped his feet on the mat. | *Her mouth fell open as she gazed at the glowing sky.
exam: Jake's plan works, and «to his amazement» he is very surprised. Why does Jake feel amazement? | Because he was hungry | Because the older boys ran away from the school | *Because the result was wonderful and hard to believe | Because his plan was boring
